        card("Activity 11: guided conversation, finding a seamstress", "You have been stationed in Barangay Tinagong Dagat, Narra, Palawan, and your new uniform needs alterations. You ask your neighbor for directions to a known seamstress or tailor. A (the soldier): ask how to get to the address; ask the street’s name; say you’re afraid you’d get lost; thank your neighbor. B (the neighbor): say it is easy, take a jeep for Barangay Bato-Bato, San Isidro, get off at the gasoline station across from the market, there’s a small street to the left of the gasoline station; say you don’t know the street’s name; emphatically say no, just follow the street until he sees a big mango tree, turn right and he will see a small eating place (karinderya) and next to it Aling Iska’s or Mang Isko’s house; say you’re welcome. A sample:", examples=dlg(_S11)),
        card("Activity 12: role play, directions to a restaurant in Tayabas", "You want to thank the Filipino family in Tayabas, Quezon who invited you for dinner by treating them to a restaurant next weekend. A friend suggested Kamayan sa Palaisdaan. You call for driving directions from your hotel and make a reservation (the book’s map and menu are left out). Student A: greet the reservations clerk, ask for landmarks and street names and make a reservation. Student B, the clerk: return the greeting, say the restaurant’s name, ask what you can do, and give specific directions including at least three landmarks, an intersection and at least two street names. A sample:", examples=dlg(_S12)),
        card("Activity 13: challenge yourself", "a. With a current map of Monterey, Carmel or Pacific Grove, be ready to ask for and give directions (at least five each) to classmates. b. With an identical map of a town, draw lots for establishments (bank, hotel, school, bus station) and give directions by landmarks (in front of, beside, next to, across from) and by starting and end points (street names, turn right or left, go straight); the class guesses which establishment it is (map-based class activities, left out)."),
